From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: widen license-files to cover udunits2

The riscv64 manylinux image carries no EPEL, so udunits2-devel (EPEL-only)
is unavailable there; the build instead compiles UDUNITS-2 from source and
auditwheel vendors the resulting libudunits2.so into the wheel. UDUNITS-2's
own BSD-style COPYRIGHT notice needs to travel with that binary, but
license-files names only cf-units' own LICENSE.

Widening the entry to a glob lets the wheel build stage UDUNITS-2's
COPYRIGHT beside LICENSE and have it land in .dist-info/licenses/.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64-only build detail: EPEL carries no udunits2-devel there, so this build alone compiles and vendors UDUNITS-2]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ name = "cf-units"
 readme = "README.md"
 requires-python = ">=3.11"
 license = "BSD-3-Clause"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE*"]

 [project.optional-dependencies]
 all = ["cf-units[docs,test]"]
